// PrintFlow — Supabase configuration template (plan task 0.1)
//
// SETUP
//   1. cp Secrets.example.xcconfig Secrets.xcconfig
//   2. Fill in the values below
//   3. Xcode → target → Build Settings → add Secrets.xcconfig as the
//      configuration file for Debug and Release
//
// Secrets.xcconfig is gitignored. This template is not. Never put a real
// key in this file.
//
// WHICH KEY: only ever the publishable/anon key. It is safe on a device
// precisely because RLS (migration 004) is what enforces access -- the key
// identifies the project, it does not grant permission. The service_role
// key bypasses RLS entirely and must never ship in an app binary.

// Local development (supabase start). These are the CLI's fixed local
// defaults, identical on every machine, and are not secrets.
SUPABASE_URL = http:/$()/127.0.0.1:54321
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0

// Production — paste from the Supabase dashboard (Project Settings → API).
// Note the $() trick above: xcconfig treats // as a comment, so a URL's
// double slash must be broken up or the value silently truncates.
// SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-publishable-key
